.TH "ELEMENT.FULLSCREENERROR_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Element.fullscreenerror_event \- Element: fullscreenerror event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]fullscreenerror\f[B]\f[R] event is fired when the browser
cannot switch to fullscreen mode.
.PP
As with the \f[CR]fullscreenchange\f[R] event, two
\f[CR]fullscreenerror\f[R] events are fired; the first is sent to the
\f[CR]Element\f[R] which failed to change modes, and the second is sent
to the \f[CR]Document\f[R] which owns that element.
.PP
For some reasons that switching into fullscreen mode might fail, see the
guide to the Fullscreen API.
.PP
This event is not cancelable.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqfullscreenerror\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onfullscreenerror = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] requestor = document.querySelector(\(dqdiv\(dq);

\f[B]function\f[R] handleError(event) {
  console.error(\(dqan error occurred changing into fullscreen\(dq);
  console.log(event);
}

requestor.addEventListener(\(dqfullscreenerror\(dq, handleError);
\f[I]// Or (but note that this replaces other event listeners\f[R]
\f[I]// added using onfullscreenerror, if any)\f[R]
requestor.onfullscreenerror = handleError;

requestor.requestFullscreen();
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]fullscreenchange\f[R]
